  "description": "On eastern boundary trees numbered from R>L from lawn end T1-Tree of Heaven(Ailanthus altissima) -reduce crown by 30%(3.5m) to suitable growth points -remove lowest inbound limb back to main stem -reduce all lateral branches to match, shape and balance T2-Western Red Cedar(Cypress-Thuja plicata) - reduce all inbound branches by up to 1.75m -RETAIN height as is T3-Tree of Heaven(Ailanthus altissima) -reduce crown by 30%(3.5m) to suitable growth points -remove lowest inbound limb back to main stem -reduce all lateral branches to match, shape and balance T4-Tree of Heaven(Ailanthus altissima) -reduce crown by 30%(3.5m) to suitable growth points -remove inbound limb overhanging roof back to main stem -cut back all highest inbound branches to reduce roof overhang T5-Tree of Heaven(Ailanthus altissima) -reduce crown by 30%(3.5m) to suitable growth points -remove inbound limb overhanging roof back to main stem -cut back all highest inbound branches to reduce roof overhang T6-Small Sycamore(Acer pseudoplatanus)-self set -section fell to ground level All works to T1 - T5 are for routine maintenance. Works to T6 are due to the tree outgrowing space",
